# punused findings adjudicated as false positives. One literal substring per
# line, matched against punused's output line; full-line `#` comments carry the
# reason. Invalid-by-construction classes: `.kiro/steering/tools.md`.
#
# MediaType and MatchMethod are named string types passed as slog attr values by
# the orchestrator's logUnmatched and logRemap, both on the production path from
# Run. main.go uses slogx.Setup's text handler, and slog.AnyValue does not
# special-case a named string type, so the attr takes the KindAny path and is
# formatted with fmt -- which dispatches to String(). Verified empirically
# against the same handler shape. Upstream: bep/punused#3.
method (MediaType).String
method (MatchMethod).String
#
# FlexInt satisfies json.Unmarshaler and is called reflectively by encoding/json.
# HistoryItem's RatingKey, Year and GrandparentRatingKey are FlexInt fields, and
# GetHistory decodes HistoryResponse on every run -- this is the load-bearing
# case, since Tautulli returns rating keys as both bare numbers and quoted
# strings.
method (*FlexInt).UnmarshalJSON
